Filed after user "branch this:archiving projects and features phase
by phase ... refined work being refined as it gets built. The idea
is not just simply throw away what doesnt have utility anymore,
we're gonna use them to create beautiful pieces of knowledge that
we acquire along the way ... we also must optimize storage. ... Like
as if they little cards structured with just the essential and it
contains all the knowledge from that project's journey ... you got
what i meant by knowledge, its the 'learned lessons' along the way."

Implements the vision documented in KB § 11.2.1 (shipped vision-only
2026-05-03 via archive-system project; this project ships the actual
implementation).

Key architectural insight: SQLite phase_learnings (shipped earlier
today via Phase enrichment loop) is the source of truth for cards.
Each per-phase learning IS a card. Distillation = SQL query +
mechanical render. No LLM needed. PROJECT.md gets lean as work
progresses (sub-task block + Improvements block removed; replaced
by one-line breadcrumb pointing to archive.md §N). Companion
archive.md grows rich phase-by-phase.

5 phases planned: single-phase MCP tool (Phase 1), --all-pending
sweep mode (Phase 2), methodology amendments + retire wish (Phase 3),
dogfood (Phase 4 distills Phases 1-3; Phase 5 distills Phase 4 +
archives the lean folder).

Builds on:
- KB § 11.2 file-level archive (shipped same day, commit c10b899).
- KB § 2.11 phase enrichment loop SQLite tracker (shipped earlier
  today, commit 2214c75).

Branch progressive-refinement-archive from origin/main per the new
"branch this" trigger order. Implementation pending user signal on
phase-by-phase cadence.

