+# progressive-refinement-archive — Project Document
+
+> **This is a living document, not a rigid checklist.**
+> As we build and learn, this project evolves. Revise phases, fold in optimizations, update §11.
+
+- **Created:** 2026-05-03
+- **Last updated:** 2026-05-03
+- **Status:** Filed → Phase 1 ready (implementation pending user signal on phase-by-phase cadence).
+- **Owner / stakeholder:** rapha (joaoraphaelsst@gmail.com)
+- **Related docs:** `KB § PATTERNS/project-execution.md § 11.2.1 Progressive refinement archiving` (the vision this project implements), `KB § PATTERNS/project-execution.md § 11.2 Archive system` (the file-level foundation shipped 2026-05-03), `KB § PATTERNS/project-execution.md § 2.11 Phase enrichment loop` (the SQLite phase_learnings store this project renders), `feedback_archive_system.md` (memory pointer for the foundation), `feedback_phase_enrichment_loop.md` (memory pointer for the learnings store).
+- **Project slug:** `progressive-refinement-archive` — cross-cutting / platform methodology + tooling project. Lives at root `projects/<slug>/`.
+- **Branch:** `progressive-refinement-archive` (per "branch this" trigger 2026-05-03).
+
+---
+
+## 1. Context & Purpose
+
+The file-level archive system shipped 2026-05-03 (`KB § PATTERNS/project-execution.md § 11.2`) replaces the auto-delete-on-close rule with auto-archive-on-close — closed projects/features move to `archive/projects/<today>/<NN>-<slug>/` via `git mv`. That preserves content + git history.
+
+But the user's vision goes further: the archive shouldn't preserve the **original tech-checklist**; it should preserve the **distilled knowledge** of the journey. **Knowledge cards** built from the per-phase learnings logged via `noctus.dev.phase_learning_log` (the SQLite tracker shipped earlier today). The PROJECT.md gets lean as work progresses; the archive grows rich; both travel together at close.
+
+User directives 2026-05-03 (combined):
+> *"what do you think about archiving projects and features phase by phase? whenever phases start to get done, blocks of the file is transported to the archived version of it? it get's lighter for future readings. And as pieces are taken out, they leave behind a one-line summary. So when projects get done, the archive gets a summarized step-by-step version of the project or the feature, of what was done and why, instead of the brute original checklist tech-file."*
+>
+> *"we also must optimize storage. ... Like as if they little cards structured with just the essential and it contains all the knowledge from that project's journey."*
+>
+> *"you got what i meant by knowledge, its the 'learned lessons' along the way."*
+
+The unifying insight (per §11.2.1): **learnings ARE the knowledge unit.** The platform already logs ≥1 non-obvious learning per phase via `noctus.dev.phase_learning_log` (per § 2.11 Phase enrichment loop). Each learning has structure: project, phase, kind (methodology / technical / process / tool / other), text. Cards = formatted learnings. Distillation = SQL query + render. No new authoring; no LLM summarization needed.
+
+The win:
+- Storage-optimized (lean PROJECT.md + dense card-shaped archive.md).
+- Browseable as a knowledge artifact (`grep -r <topic> archive/projects/*/*/archive.md`).
+- Future agents picking up similar work read the journey's lessons in compact form.
+- Leverages existing infrastructure (SQLite phase_learnings + file-level archive).
+
+---
+
+## 2. Confirmed constraints
+
+- **Cards are formatted learnings.** Source of truth = `mcp/noctusai/data/phase_learnings.db`. The renderer reads that table; doesn't re-author. *(Drives §3 principle 1 + §6 Phase 2.)*
+- **Per-phase distillation triggers at phase close** — after the per-phase commit lands. Fallback: PROJECT-close sweep (`--all-pending`) for skipped phases. *(Drives §6 Phase 3.)*
+- **PROJECT.md edited atomically** — the phase's sub-task block + Improvements block removed; one-line breadcrumb inserted. Companion `archive.md` appended with rendered cards. Both edits stage for the agent to commit (or commit inline). *(Drives §6 Phase 2 — edit-in-place tooling.)*
+- **No LLM summarization required.** Learnings were authored intentionally at phase close; rendering is mechanical. *(Drives §3 principle 2 — no LLM dependency in v1.)*
+- **Storage optimization is a side effect, not a goal.** The card shape happens to be compact; that's a feature, not the premise. The premise is knowledge artifact quality. *(Drives §3 principle 3.)*
+- **Builds on top of file-level archive.** The companion `archive.md` lives in `projects/<slug>/` during execution, then travels to `archive/projects/<today>/<NN>-<slug>/archive.md` via the existing § 11.2 close-gate. *(Drives §8 dependencies.)*
+
+---
+
+## 3. Design principles
+
+1. **SQLite phase_learnings is the single source of truth for cards.** The renderer queries; doesn't compose. If a phase has 0 learnings logged, it has 0 cards (and the breadcrumb says so — "0 cards · phase missed enrichment loop"). Per-phase enrichment-loop discipline (§ 2.11) becomes the input quality gate for this system.
+2. **Mechanical rendering, no LLM in v1.** Cards are formatted from structured DB rows. LLM-based summarization could enhance later (e.g. cross-phase synthesis, theme tagging) — out of v1 scope.
+3. **Card content > storage size.** The point is the journey's lessons in a compact form, not raw byte savings. Storage optimization is a happy side effect.
+4. **Atomic PROJECT.md edits.** The breadcrumb-swap operation (remove sub-task block + Improvements block; insert breadcrumb line) must be transactional. Markdown parsing required (consider `markdown-it-py` or `mistune`); regex on heading lines is too brittle.
+5. **Per-phase preferred; PROJECT-close sweep as fallback.** Live distillation matches the user's "as work progresses" framing. The sweep mode exists for missed phases, not as the default.
+6. **Idempotency.** Re-running `archive_phase` on a phase that's already been distilled should detect the existing breadcrumb and refuse (same shape as `noctus.dev.archive`'s already-archived guard).
+
+---
+
+## 3a. Seed-first analysis (REQUIRED — the seed is every product's skeleton)
+
+1. **Is the contract identical for every product?** N/A — this is platform-level methodology + tooling, not product code.
+2. **Is the data source product-specific?** N/A.
+3. **Is the placement product-specific?** N/A.
+4. **Is the visibility / permission rule the same?** N/A.
+5. **Does the seam already exist in seed?** No — this is dev-toolkit territory.
+6. **Default-on or opt-in?** **Default-on once landed.** Methodology applies platform-wide (every project/feature uses progressive refinement at close).
+
+**Litmus — per-product code count this design requires:** [x] **0 lines** in any `products/<x>/` tree. All work lands in `mcp/noctusai/`, `KNOWLEDGE-BASE/`, `CLAUDE/`, agent memory.
+
+**Phase plan implications:** §6 phases work in dev-toolkit + KB + CLAUDE. **No phase walks through products.** Correct shape.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Scope
+
+**In scope:**
+
+- Phase 1 — `mcp/noctusai/tools/noctus/dev/archive_phase.py` — MCP tool `noctus.dev.archive_phase` that:
+  - Queries `phase_learnings` for `(project_slug, phase_number)`.
+  - Renders the rows as cards in markdown (per §5.2 card format).
+  - Edits PROJECT.md atomically: removes phase sub-task block + Improvements block; inserts breadcrumb line.
+  - Appends rendered cards to companion `archive.md` (creates if missing).
+  - Idempotency guard: detects existing breadcrumb; refuses if phase already distilled.
+- Phase 2 — `--all-pending` sweep mode for the tool: distills every closed-but-undistilled phase in a project at once.
+- Phase 3 — Tests in `mcp/noctusai/tests/test_archive_phase.py` covering: render, breadcrumb-swap, archive.md append, missing-learnings case, idempotency, sweep mode.
+- Phase 4 — Methodology amendments: §11.2.1 of `project-execution.md` updated from "vision; deferred" to "shipped" with recipe references; CLAUDE/projects.md amended; new `feedback_progressive_refinement_archive.md` memory entry; delete `wish_implement_progressive_refinement_archive.md` + index update.
+- Phase 5 — Project close: dogfood the new tool on this project's own phases (each Phase 1-4 distilled into cards before close); orchestrator merge to main.
+
+**Out of scope (for now — with reason):**
+
+- **LLM-based card synthesis** (e.g. cross-phase theme detection, narrative summarization). v1 is mechanical; LLM enhancement is a future enhancement project.
+- **Card search tooling** (e.g. an MCP tool that searches across all archived projects' cards). v1 ships rendering; search is `grep` for now.
+- **Card export** (e.g. tag/kind aggregation across projects). Future enhancement.
+- **Backfilling cards for already-archived projects** (the projects archived today + tomorrow without progressive refinement). The existing PROJECT.md preserved in those archives is fine; backfill is low value + high effort.
+- **Hook integration** (auto-run `archive_phase` at phase commit via pre-commit hook). v1 is manual invocation; auto-trigger is a future enhancement.
+- **PROJECT.md schema validation** (formal markdown schema for §6 phase blocks). v1 uses heading-anchored parsing; schema validation is a hardening pass.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Architecture / Data Model
+
+### 5.1 The `archive.md` companion file
+
+Lives at `projects/<slug>/archive.md` during execution. Built up phase-by-phase as `archive_phase` runs. Travels with the project to `archive/projects/<today>/<NN>-<slug>/archive.md` via the § 11.2 close-gate.
+
+Header section (always present):
+
+```markdown
+# <project-slug> — Knowledge cards
+
+Distilled from per-phase learnings logged to `mcp/noctusai/data/phase_learnings.db` per
+`KB § PATTERNS/project-execution.md § 2.11 Phase enrichment loop` and rendered per
+`§ 11.2.1 Progressive refinement archiving`.
+```
+
+Per-phase section (appended on each `archive_phase` call):
+
+```markdown
+## Phase N — <title>
+
+Shipped: <date>. Commit: <hash>. <K> cards.
+
+### Card N.1 [<kind>]
+> <learning_text wrapped in blockquote>
+> _commit <hash> · learning id=<row_id>_
+
+### Card N.2 [<kind>]
+> ...
+```
+
+### 5.2 Card format (rendered per learning row)
+
+| Field in SQLite row | Mapping in card |
+|---|---|
+| `phase_number` | Section header level (`## Phase N`) |
+| `phase_title` | Section header text |
+| `learning_kind` | Card subheading tag `[<kind>]` |
+| `learning_text` | Blockquote body |
+| `shipped_at` (ISO timestamp) | Phase header "Shipped: <date>" line (date portion only) |
+| `created_by` | (omitted from rendered card; available via SQL query) |
+| `consumed_by_phase_number` | (omitted; consumption is a methodology concern, not knowledge content) |
+
+The `commit hash` for the card footer comes from `git log` querying the project's branch for the commit closest to `shipped_at` (heuristic) OR is passed explicitly as a tool parameter if the agent knows it.
+
+### 5.3 PROJECT.md breadcrumb format
+
+Where `### Phase N — <title> ✅` previously had sub-tasks + Improvements blocks below it, after distillation:
+
+```markdown
+### Phase N — <title> ✅ → archive.md §N · 2 cards (1 methodology, 1 technical) · commit 216cc1a
+```
+
+The breadcrumb line replaces the sub-task block. The phase header itself stays (status icon, title). Other phase content (the trailing prose like "Phase 6 dogfooded...") stays IF it's not a sub-task or Improvements bullet.
+
+### 5.4 MCP tool: `noctus.dev.archive_phase`
+
+```python
+def archive_phase(
+    project_slug: str,
+    phase_number: int | None = None,    # if None, requires --all-pending
+    all_pending: bool = False,           # sweep mode
+    project_md_path: str | None = None,  # default: projects/<slug>/PROJECT.md (or products/.../projects/<slug>/PROJECT.md)
+    archive_md_path: str | None = None,  # default: alongside PROJECT.md
+    commit_hash: str | None = None,      # explicit commit for the card footer; fallback to git log heuristic
+    repo_root: Path | None = None,       # tests
+) -> dict:
+    """Distill phase learnings to cards in archive.md; insert breadcrumb in PROJECT.md.
+
+    Returns:
+      {
+        "phases_distilled": [<int>, ...],         # phase numbers acted on
+        "cards_rendered": int,                     # total cards across phases acted on
+        "archive_md_path": "<relative path>",
+        "project_md_path": "<relative path>",
+      }
+    """
+```
+
+### 5.5 Markdown parsing approach
+
+Phase blocks in PROJECT.md follow a predictable structure: heading at `### Phase N — <title>`, content until next `### ` or `---`. The tool can:
+- Use `markdown-it-py` or `mistune` to AST-parse PROJECT.md, find the phase block, replace it.
+- OR string-based with anchored regex on `### Phase N` headings and section delimiters. Higher risk of edge-case bugs (nested code blocks with `### ` inside, etc.).
+
+Recommended: `markdown-it-py` (already in some Python environments; minimal dep) for safety. Investigate at Phase 1.
+
